 "generatorWeaknesses": [
  "PlaytestTest builds PLACE_REL fixtures with SpatialWorlds, which puts the anchor down as a block. A creature anchor (주민 뒤에 / 고양이 옆에 / 말 옆에) fails there (\"fixture does not satisfy BEHIND for villager\", NEXT_TO a cat did not advance), so no placement next to a creature could ship although the generator and the sensor support it. The creature-anchored steps drafted for adv_adventure_trade, familienpfad, w3_05 and w3_07 became block-anchored ones.",
  "PlaytestTest plays a SEQUENCE part by part for three ticks each, with no baseline tick and no clock: a sequence with an ACQUIRE_ITEM, TRANSIT or MOUNT part cannot be driven (uhrmacher s1, w3_05 s1, w3_07 s1 were drafted that way and became plain steps). -고 with instant parts (USE_BLOCK, PLACE, CRAFT, TAKE_OUT, GIVE, INTERACT) plays fine.",
  "USE_BLOCK on a sign says 표지판을 사용하세요 (글을 써요 only with ink in hand). An authored 표지판에 이름을 쓰세요 fails authoredCluesNameTheAction (the verb of the goal is 사용/글을 쓰다, not 쓰다 alone) and 이름 \"does not describe the goal\", so 이름 (name) has no step to live in.",
  "A tag anchor with no word of its own is spoken 그것 (#minecraft:signs, #minecraft:candles), so a later step cannot point back at \"the sign\" with a tag; a specific id is spoken with its wood or colour (자작나무 표지판, 주황색 초).",
  "tools/coverage.py reads 파세요 (팔다 -ㄹ drop) as 파다, so a TRADE SELL clue never teaches 팔다 and the hint 팔아요 is \"unknown\" until 팔다 has met three other encounters; two authored finale lines carry them (glockenpfad, uhrmacher).",
  "HEAR knows a jukebox and a note block, not a bell, so the brief's \"듣다 with the bell\" is not possible; the bell is USE_BLOCK (종을 울리세요). A HEAR step on a note block would need the trail to hand out redstone.",
  "The (verb, object) ratchet counts block ids, and torch (PLACE x6), campfire (KINDLE x6), candle (STAND x5), cobblestone (STACK x5) and oak sign (STAND x4) are full; lantern, flower pot, chest, barrel, crafting table, white carpet, apple and bread are at three. Placement steps had to use wood, colour and flower variants (birch sign, orange tulip, light gray carpet) to stay under it.",
  "TRADE and INTERACT_ENTITY have no deciding form, so a buy or sale and a talk with 주민과 never count as form-dependent although they practise 에게서/에게 and 하고/와/과. No goal counts people, so 주민 두 명 (L2.counter_more for 명) cannot be said in a clue.",
  "Only 4 of the 15 finale lines are authored (glockenpfad, uhrmacher, zuhausepfad, familienpfad), but the 70% generated-finale rule has little slack left (300 of 422 generated, 296 needed)."
 ],
 "openIssues": [
  "Target words with no home in a clue, hint or finale: 이름, 창문, 아이, 방, 시간, 돈, 그림, 받다, 만나다, 부르다, 듣다, 읽다, 쓰다 (write). 가족 and 창문 have no concept entry; 가족 is only in the familienpfad finale text.",
  "Reachability assumptions: a village for the bell, the villagers and the market; gold and redstone for the clock (uhrmacher, in reach per ReachabilityGateTest); a tamed cat (familienpfad follows haustierpfad); a horse near the gate (w3_07 follows reitpfad); carrots from a farm (w3_06); emeralds from marktpfad for the purchase in handelsstrasse (it follows marktpfad); fifteen coal for the one sale in adv_adventure_trade (armorer, toolsmith, butcher and fisherman villagers buy it).",
  "adv_adventure_trade has one real TRADE (selling coal), as its advancement asks; handelsstrasse has the only purchase.",
  "w3_05 follows sternenhaus, which is still in reachabilityDebt.",
  "uhrmacher s2 stacks cobblestone, a (verb, object) pair that was already over three (4 to 5); the maximum stays 6."
 ],
